 "notes": [
  "First quarter with IHS Markit for the full period in both GAAP and adjusted results; current-quarter adjusted figures are actual scope (no pro forma / divestiture lines). Comparatives (Q1-22) are pro forma / non-GAAP pro forma adjusted (adjusted EPS growth +9% vs PF 2.89).",
  "Segments: MI, Ratings, Commodity Insights (CI), Mobility (MOB), Indices, Engineering Solutions (ES, held for sale; still consolidated, not discontinued) + Equity in Income on Unconsolidated Subsidiaries line.",
  "Gain on dispositions (50) = gain: gain_disp = +50. 'Other expense (income), net' printed 11 = EXPENSE: oth_inc = -11. Loss on extinguishment of debt \u2014 (0).",
  "Segment expense table total 2,016 vs IS expenses 2,080 (segment table nets gains and equity income).",
  "CI footnote items sum 15 vs printed 14 (rounding). Mobility IHS Markit merger costs after-tax printed as 'less than $1 million' (net omitted).",
  "New NONOP item: premium amortization benefit of $7m ($5m after-tax) in interest expense (adjusted interest 92 vs reported 85).",
  "Footnote after-tax items sum to 10 vs aggregate 9 (rounding); 795 + 10 + 209 = 1,014 vs adjusted NI 1,013.",
  "Indices adjusted operating profit attributable to the Company: 184 (adjusted NCI share 61).",
  "corp_nongaap / corp_deal_amort in add-back sign (reduce unallocated expense).",
  "cfpub three months; capex and nci_dist recorded as positive outflows; adjusted FCF = 'Non-GAAP pro forma adjusted free cash flow excluding certain items' 662.",
  "No organic table: reported revenue +3% vs Q1-22 pro forma revenue (3,072), +4% constant currency (narrative); rev_cc_organic_growth_pct = 4 is on that basis.",
  "FCF guidance cut by ~$100m for IRC Section 174 R&D capitalisation cash-tax impact (prior guidance $4.3-$4.4bn).",
  "items_total_pre (41) is the operating-profit 'Non-GAAP adjustments' line; the interest adjustment (premium amortization, 7) is shown separately in the interest table."
 ],
